IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-principles`

-- ccc20-tests-principles.l4 -- tests for ccc20-part16-principles.l4 (ss 493.1, 493.11, 493.2). Expected values are hand-written from the text of lines 11057-11072.

§ `Tests -- section 493.1: the principle of restraint`
-- args: the decision-maker; the decision is made under this Part; the answer of 493.11(2)(c) (the accused is one to whom 515(6), 522(2), 523(2.1) or 524(4) applies)
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a peace officer` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a peace officer` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a peace officer` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a justice` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a judge` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a justice` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a judge` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a justice` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a judge` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a peace officer` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a justice` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `the prosecutor` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the peace officer, justice or judge must give primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity and on the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `the prosecutor` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the decision-maker must take into account the grounds referred to in subsection 498(1.1) or 515(10), as the case may be` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.1 the decision-maker must take into account the grounds referred to in subsection 498(1.1) or 515(10), as the case may be` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 493.11: clarification and application`
-- (1) the text says in its own words that section 493.1 does not require the accused to be released
#ASSERT `s 493.11(1) section 493.1 requires the accused to be released` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(a) args: the decision-maker; the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that detention is necessary in the public interest under 498(1.1)
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(a) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused` `a peace officer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(a) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused` `a peace officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(a) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused` `a justice` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(a) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused` `the prosecutor` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(b) args: the decision-maker; the peace officer releases the accused
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(b) the peace officer must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a peace officer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(b) the peace officer must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a peace officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(b) the peace officer must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(b) namely: the condition is necessary to address the risks as they relate to the purposes of 501(3)
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(b) the condition is one of the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(b) the condition is one of the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(c) args: the decision-maker; one answer each of s 515(6), s 522(2), s 523(2.1), s 524(4)
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(c) the justice or judge is barred from giving primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity` `a justice` (LIST (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(c) the justice or judge is barred from giving primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity` `a judge` (LIST (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(c) the justice or judge is barred from giving primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity` `a justice` (LIST (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(c) the justice or judge is barred from giving primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity` `a justice` (LIST (JUST FALSE), NOTHING, (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(c) the justice or judge is barred from giving primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity` `a justice` (LIST NOTHING, (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(c) the justice or judge is barred from giving primary consideration to the release of the accused at the earliest reasonable opportunity` `a peace officer` (LIST (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(d) args: the decision-maker; the justice or judge releases the accused
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(d) the justice or judge must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(d) the justice or judge must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a judge` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(d) the justice or judge must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a justice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(d) the justice or judge must impose the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` `a peace officer` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(d) the condition is one of the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(d) the condition is one of the least onerous conditions that are appropriate in the circumstances` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(e) args: the decision-maker; the answer of s 515(10): the detention of the accused is justified
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(e) the justice or judge is barred from ordering that the accused be released` `a justice` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(e) the justice or judge is barred from ordering that the accused be released` `a judge` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(e) the justice or judge is barred from ordering that the accused be released` `a justice` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(e) the justice or judge is barred from ordering that the accused be released` `a judge` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 493.11(2)(e) the justice or judge is barred from ordering that the accused be released` `a peace officer` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 493.2: Aboriginal accused and vulnerable populations`
#ASSERT `s 493.2(a) the accused is an Aboriginal accused, to whose circumstances particular attention must be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.2(a) the accused is an Aboriginal accused, to whose circumstances particular attention must be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.2(b) the accused belongs to a vulnerable population, to whose circumstances particular attention must be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.2(b) the accused belongs to a vulnerable population, to whose circumstances particular attention must be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- composite args: the decision-maker; the decision is made under this Part; the answer of (a); the answer of (b)
#ASSERT `s 493.2 the peace officer, justice or judge must give particular attention to the circumstances of the accused` `a justice` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.2 the peace officer, justice or judge must give particular attention to the circumstances of the accused` `a judge` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.2 the peace officer, justice or judge must give particular attention to the circumstances of the accused` `a peace officer` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.2 the peace officer, justice or judge must give particular attention to the circumstances of the accused` `a peace officer` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 493.2 the peace officer, justice or judge must give particular attention to the circumstances of the accused` `a peace officer` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.2 the peace officer, justice or judge must give particular attention to the circumstances of the accused` `the prosecutor` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
